  "notes": [
    "Early pure runner tests pulled Tauri runtime symbols into the test executable and failed at load. Inject an event sink into the service; production alone binds Tauri. No executable-manifest workaround remains.",
    "Initial real-ffmpeg tests exposed a short job finishing before the periodic sample and a process-attachment wait. Push the final observed timestamp and a process-attached zero event, retain actual cancel percentage, and wait for actual attachment before cancelling. Final owned test also proves bundled repair with an invalid old preferred engine and an unreachable proxy.",
    "One full serial run stopped with STATUS_STACK_BUFFER_OVERRUN in the unchanged privacy registry fixture. Its exact isolated rerun, direct full serial rerun and complete e/f gates pass. Original failed log is retained; no privacy exception or out-of-scope production change was added.",
    "Initial screenshot pairs had identical visible/expanded DOM, opacity, finished animations and IPC but differed in raster output after focused controls. Preserve failed image pairs/DOM diagnostics. Final capture uses a single CDP session, explicit matching device metrics, persistent transparent background and naturally settled animation; no product state, time or CSS freeze. Final 36 tool and eight Settings captures repeat exactly at actual1x/1.5x.",
    "The older unrelated Clear history danger button has a3.88 contrast finding in the first whole Settings viewport. Final new-section evidence top-aligns Files/licences and retains all default axe rules. This is not a claim of whole Settings accessibility.",
    "A real review-navigation bug could reopen remembered Search when Tool jobs or file review requested another view. Clear remembered Search for explicit review/focus routes and extend the existing StrictMode regression test. Native result-to-queue path exercises it.",
    "Initial local-only input test disguised a playlist as mov, which upstream already rejected; final valid m3u8 fixture uses a working permissive loopback control and verifies zero requests under the actual whitelist.",
    "All failed/interim logs and captures remain; only named final reports establish acceptance. Earlier v51-v56 evidence is unchanged. No accessibility exclusion, lint suppression, secret waiver, real clipboard/global input, hosted account/profile or OS setting change."
  ]
}
